ly:[`Activate Assembly`,`Sets an assembly as the active one for editing.`],Assembly_CreateAssembly:[`New Assembly`,`Creates an assembly object in the current document, or in the current active assembly (if any). Limit of one root assembly per file.`],Assembly_CreateBom:[`Bill of Materials`,`<p>Creates a bill of materials of the current assembly. If an assembly is active, it will be a BOM of this assembly. Else it will be a BOM of the whole document.</p><p>The BOM object is a document object that stores the settings of your BOM. It is also a spreadsheet object so you can easily visualize the BOM. If you do not need the BOM object to be saved as a document object, you can simply export and cancel the task.</p><p>The columns 'Index', 'Name', 'File Name' and 'Quantity' are automatically generated on recompute. The 'Description' and custom columns are not overwritten.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointAngle:[`Angle Joint`,`Creates an angle joint that fixes the angle between the Z-axis of the selected coordinate systems`],Assembly_CreateJointBall:[`Ball Joint`,`Creates a ball joint that connects parts at a point, allowing unrestricted movement as long as the connection points remain in contact`],Assembly_CreateJointCylindrical:[`Cylindrical Joint`,`Creates a cylindrical joint that allows rotation around and translation along a single axis between assembled parts`],Assembly_CreateJointDistance:[`Distance Joint`,`<p>Creates a distance joint that fixes the distance between the selected objects</p><p>Creates one of several different joints based on the selection. For example, a distance of 0 between a plane and a cylinder creates a tangent joint. A distance of 0 between planes will make them co-planar.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointFixed:[`Fixed Joint`,`<p>1 - If an assembly is active : Creates a joint statically locking two parts together, preventing any movement or rotation</p><p>2 - If a part is active: Positions sub-parts by matching selected coordinate systems. The second part selected will move.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointGearBelt:[`Gears/Belt Joint`,`<p>Creates a gears or belt joint that links 2 rotating gears together</p><p>Select the same coordinate systems as the revolute joints.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointGears:[`Gears Joint`,`<p>Creates a gears joint that links 2 rotating gears together. They will have inverse rotation direction.</p><p>Select the same coordinate systems as the revolute joints.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointParallel:[`Parallel Joint`,`Creates a parallel joint that makes the Z-axis of the selected coordinate systems parallel`],Assembly_CreateJointPerpendicular:[`Perpendicular Joint`,`Creates a perpendicular joint that makes the Z-axis of the selected coordinate systems perpendicular`],Assembly_CreateJointRackPinion:[`Rack and Pinion Joint`,`<p>Creates a rack and pinion joint that links a part with a slider joint to a part with a revolute joint</p><p>Select the same coordinate systems as the revolute and slider joints. The pitch radius defines the movement ratio between the rack and the pinion.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointRevolute:[`Revolute Joint`,`Creates a revolute joint allowing rotation around a single axis between selected parts`],Assembly_CreateJointRigidGroup:[`Create Rigid Group`,`<p>Create a rigid group.</p><p>Creates a rigid group that permanently locks the selected components together.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointScrew:[`Screw Joint`,`<p>Creates a screw joint that links a part with a slider joint to a part with a revolute joint</p><p>Select the same coordinate systems as the revolute and slider joints. The pitch radius defines the movement ratio between the rotating screw and the sliding part.</p>`],Assembly_CreateJointSlider:[`Slider Joint`,`Creates a slider joint that allows linear movement along a single axis, but restricts rotation between selected parts`],Assembly_CreateSimulation:[`Simulation`,`Creates a new simulation of the current assembly`],Assembly_CreateSnapshot:[`Snapshot`,`Captures the current assembly state (placements and visibility). Double-clicking the Snapshot object restores the assembly to that state.`],Assembly_CreateView:[`Exploded View`,`Creates an exploded view of the current assembly`],Assembly_ExportASMT:[`Export ASMT File`,`Export currently active assembly as a ASMT file.`],Assembly_Insert:[`Insert Component`,`<p>Inserts a component into the active assembly. This will create dynamic links to parts, bodies, primitives, and assemblies. To insert external components, make sure that the file is <b>open in the current session</b></p><ul><li>Insert by left clicking items in the list.</li><li>Remove by right clicking items in the list.</li><li>Press shift to add several instances of the component while clicking on the view.</li></ul>`],Assembly_InsertLink:[`Insert Component`,`<p>Inserts a component into the active assembly. This will create dynamic links to parts, bodies, primitives, and assemblies. To insert external components, make sure that the file is <b>open in the current session</b></p><ul><li>Insert by left clicking items in the list.</li><li>Remove by right clicking items in the list.</li><li>Press shift to add several instances of the component while clicking on the view.</li></ul>`],Assembly_InsertNewPart:[`New Part`,`Insert a new part into the active assembly. The new part's origin can be positioned in the assembly.`],Assembly_LinkSelectLinked:[`Go to Linked Assembly`,`Selects the linked assembly and switches to its original document`],Assembly_SelectJointsOfComponent:[`Select Component Joints`,`Selects all joints referencing the selected component`],Assembly_SolveAssembly:[`Solve Assembly`,`Solves the currently active assembly.`],Assembly_ToggleGrounded:[`Toggle Grounded`,`<p>Toggles the grounding of a part.</p><p>Grounding a part permanently locks its position in the assembly, preventing any movement or rotation.`],PartDesign_AdditiveHelix:[`Additive Helix`,`Sweeps the selected sketch or profile along a helix and adds it to the body`],PartDesign_